        <body>
            <div xml:id="d577">

                <pb facs="0702" n="388" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg388"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/725</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Van Dyke</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                        ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                        notAfter="1914-10-11T23:00:00-05:00" notBefore="1914-10-11T00:00:00+00:19"
                            ><hi rendition="#italic">undated</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Received October 11, 11 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>44. Replying your 33, Foreign Minister says Government will receive oil cakes as
                    consigned. Holland-America Line for present will ship only goods consigned to
                    Government and which may not be exported. List of exports prohibited follows
                    soon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Van Dyke</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
